      "updated_at": "2026-09-23T08:54:27Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "approach ACK\n\nusing `optional<size_t>` here clearly separates the \"no `Content-Length`\" case\nfrom the `Content-Length: 0` case; previously both were represented as a plain\n`size_t` defaulting to `0`, which made \"_absent_\" and \"_present-but-zero_\"\nindistinguishable and caused a hang, since the client would wait on the peer to\nclose the connection even though it had already signaled an empty body\n\nmakes sense overall, as does the revert to the old timeout behaviour ",
